-- title:
--   Vélu discriminant identity for odd-order kernels
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field and $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $F$ with invertible discriminant (`W.IsElliptic`), let $n$ be a natural number and let $Q$ be a point of the associated affine curve `W.toAffine` whose order in the group of points is exactly $2n+1$. Let $S =$ `W.oddOrderSummingSet Q n` be the finite subset of $F \times F$ obtained as the image of the integers $1 \le k \le n$ under $k \mapsto$ `coordsOrZero` $(k \bullet Q)$, i.e. the set of coordinate pairs $(x,y)$ of the multiples $kQ$ for $1 \le k \le n$ (the point at infinity, should it occur, contributing the pair $(0,0)$). Let `W.veluQuotient S` be the Weierstrass curve with the same $a_1, a_2, a_3$ as $W$ and with $a_4$ replaced by $a_4 - 5\sum_{P \in S}$ `W.veluT` $P_1 P_2$ and $a_6$ replaced by $a_6 - b_2 \sum_{P \in S}$ `W.veluT` $P_1 P_2 - 7\sum_{P \in S}$ `W.veluW` $P_1 P_2$. Then the discriminant of `W.veluQuotient S`, multiplied by the fourth power of $\prod_{P \in S}$ `W.veluU` $P_1 P_2$, where `W.veluU` $x\,y = (2y + a_1 x + a_3)^2$, equals $\Delta(W)^{2n+1}$.
--
--   This is the exact multiplicative form, signs included, of the transformation of the discriminant under Vélu's model of the quotient of $W$ by the cyclic group generated by a point of odd order $2n+1$, the factor $\prod_{P} u_P$ accounting for the weight. It is used in the treatment of the Tate criterion for the Vélu quotient and in the construction of integral models and enumerations of cyclic quotients with non-vanishing discriminant.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_veluQuotient_oddOrderSummingSet_discriminant_prod_veluU_pow.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_Velu
import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_OddOrderSummingSet

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open WeierstrassCurve

theorem WeierstrassCurve.veluQuotient_oddOrderSummingSet_discriminant_prod_veluU_pow
    {F : Type*} [Field F] [DecidableEq F] (W : WeierstrassCurve F) [W.IsElliptic]
    {n : ℕ} (Q : W.toAffine.Point) (hQ : addOrderOf Q = 2 * n + 1) :
    (W.veluQuotient (W.oddOrderSummingSet Q n)).Δ *
        (∏ P ∈ W.oddOrderSummingSet Q n, W.veluU P.1 P.2) ^ 4
      = W.Δ ^ (2 * n + 1) := by sorry
